{%- comment -%}
  Price drop — the discount, stated once, computed from the product.

  ZERO MAINTENANCE IS THE WHOLE DESIGN. Nothing here is typed: not the price, not the old
  price, not the percentage, not the saving. Every number is read from the product at
  render time, so putting the price back up needs no edit anywhere. The moment
  compare-at stops being higher than price — because the price went up, or because the
  compare-at was cleared — this block renders nothing at all and vanishes from the page.
  A sale badge that has to be remembered is a sale badge that eventually lies.

  THE REASON LINE MUST NOT CONTAIN A PRICE. It is the one field a human writes, and the
  temptation is to put the figures in it — "back to $29.99 soon". Do that and the whole
  design is undone: the block keeps its numbers current automatically and that sentence
  does not, so the day the price moves the page contradicts itself. Say why, and say that
  it ends. Let the computed parts say how much.

  IT FAILS CLOSED. If an end date is set and that date has passed, the block stops
  rendering rather than quietly carrying on. The classic dark pattern is the offer that
  keeps announcing itself after it ended, or the timer that resets on refresh; the only
  way to be sure this never does either is to make expiry mean disappear.

  WHAT IT DELIBERATELY IS NOT. No stock counter — the product is a file, there is no
  scarcity and claiming one would be a lie. No ticking clock. This shop sells to people
  whose condition runs on urgency and doubt, and a countdown works by manufacturing
  exactly the pressure these workbooks exist to unwind. A real deadline stated as a date
  is honest and does the same job; a clock counting down milliseconds is theatre aimed at
  the nervous system.

  AN UNEXPLAINED DISCOUNT ARGUES AGAINST YOU. Ninety per cent off a digital product reads
  as "this is what it is worth", not "this is a bargain". The reason is what makes a large
  discount believable, which is why this block would rather show no percentage than no
  reason.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign product = closest.product
  assign price = product.price
  assign was = product.compare_at_price

  assign on_sale = false
  if was > price and price > 0
    assign on_sale = true
  endif

  comment
    An end date that has passed takes the whole block down with it. Compared at the end
    of the named day, in the shop's timezone, so "ends the 30th" includes the 30th.
  endcomment
  assign expired = false
  if block.settings.ends_at != blank
    assign now_stamp = 'now' | date: '%s' | plus: 0
    assign end_stamp = block.settings.ends_at | date: '%s' | plus: 86399
    if now_stamp > end_stamp
      assign expired = true
    endif
  endif
-%}

{%- if on_sale and expired == false -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign saved = was | minus: price
    assign percent = saved | times: 100.0 | divided_by: was | round
    assign accent = block.settings.accent | default: '#39FF14'
  -%}

  <div class="pdr" style="--pdr-accent:{{ accent }};" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
    <p class="pdr__row">
      {%- if block.settings.show_percent -%}
        <span class="pdr__pill">{{ percent }}% off</span>
      {%- endif -%}
      <span class="pdr__saved">You save {{ saved | money }}</span>
    </p>

    {%- if block.settings.reason != blank -%}
      <p class="pdr__reason">{{ block.settings.reason | escape }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if block.settings.ends_at != blank -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Only claim a deadline when there is one. The date and the old price are both read
        from live data, so neither can drift out of step with what is actually charged.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <p class="pdr__ends">
        Back to {{ was | money }} after {{ block.settings.ends_at | date: '%-d %B' }}.
      </p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  {%- style -%}
    .pdr { margin: 2px 0 0; color: inherit; }

    .pdr__row {
      margin: 0;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 8px;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
    }

    /* The one loud element on the page, and it is loud because it is true. */
    .pdr__pill {
      background: var(--pdr-accent);
      color: #0B0F0D;
      font-size: .68rem;
      font-weight: 800;
      letter-spacing: .07em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      padding: 3px 9px;
      border-radius: 999px;
      white-space: nowrap;
    }

    .pdr__saved {
      font-size: .82rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    }

    .pdr__reason { margin: 6px 0 0; font-size: .8rem; line-height: 1.45; opacity: .78; }
    .pdr__ends { margin: 3px 0 0; font-size: .76rem; line-height: 1.45; opacity: .6; }
  {%- endstyle -%}
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Price drop",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Reads the product's price and compare-at price. Every number is computed, so nothing here needs editing when the price changes — and the block disappears on its own the moment the product is no longer discounted."
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "reason",
      "label": "Why it's this price",
      "default": "We're new. The price is low while we find our first customers — it goes back up after that.",
      "info": "The only line a human writes. Keep prices OUT of it — the figures above update themselves, this sentence would not. Say why it is low and that it ends."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "ends_at",
      "label": "Last day of the offer",
      "info": "YYYY-MM-DD. Optional. Leave empty for no deadline. If the date passes, the whole block stops showing rather than claiming an offer that has ended."
    },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_percent", "label": "Show the percentage", "default": true },
    { "type": "color", "id": "accent", "label": "Accent colour", "default": "#39FF14" }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Price drop" }]
}
{% endschema %}
